title: Genesis 18 – The Judge of All the Earth
description: A verse-by-verse study of Genesis 18: the LORD appears to Abraham in the plains of Mamre, Christ in the Old Testament, Sarah laughs, is any thing too hard for the LORD, and Abraham intercedes for Sodom.
output: lessons/genesis/genesis-18-the-judge-of-all-the-earth.html
context: Genesis 18

# Genesis series pattern (Genesis 1-5). Slide text is the author's own sentences from the Genesis 18 study (posts
# 6976, 6977, 7 December 2022), set in chapter order. Verses the study typed are shown from the KJV.
# Fixed: "As the Bible says in James 5, *behold, the Judge is standing right at the door.*" quoted the verse in other
# words; put back to the KJV, "*behold, the judge standeth before the door.*" (6976). Nothing else.

=== Introduction
--- Genesis Chapter 18 [title]
overline: Young Adult Sunday School • Genesis Series
heading: Genesis 18: The Judge of All the Earth
sub: The LORD Appears to Abraham • Sarah Laughed • Abraham Intercedes for Sodom
refs: Genesis 18:1-33
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any reference to read the verse.

=== In the plains of Mamre
--- The LORD Appeared unto Him
kicker: vv. 1–2
sub: Three Men Stood by Him
scripture: Genesis 18:1-2 | mark: And the LORD appeared unto him
p: This is an Old Testament manifestation of Christ Jesus, appearing with two messengers, angels of the Lord before Abraham on their way to judge Sodom and Gomorrah.

--- My LORD, Pass Not Away
kicker: vv. 3–5
sub: Rest Yourselves under the Tree
scripture: Genesis 18:3-5 | mark: My LORD, if now I have found favour in thy sight
p: Seeing them approach, Abraham recognizes Him, and runs to prepare a meal, and give hospitality to God and His angels.

--- A Calf Tender and Good
kicker: vv. 6–8
sub: And They Did Eat
scripture: Genesis 18:6-8 | mark: and they did eat

--- No Man Hath Seen God at Any Time
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 18:1
fig: John 1:18 | John 1:18
callout: We can know this is Jesus, by comparing scripture with scripture. But as we have seen repeatedly in the OT, the Lord, the word of God, and here, "Judge of all the earth" appears before Abraham and Sarah, talking with them and eating. Abraham recognizes Him right away.

--- The Judge of Quick and Dead
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 18:25
fig: Acts 10:42 | Acts 10:42
fig: 2 Corinthians 5:10 | 2 Corinthians 5:10
callout: The Bible says Jesus is the Judge of all the earth.

--- The Judge Standeth before the Door
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 18:1
fig: James 5:9 | James 5:9
callout: As the Bible says in James 5, *behold, the judge standeth before the door.* Just as He was before the door of the tent of Abraham, on the plains of Mamre, West of Sodom.

=== Sarah laughed
--- Sarah Shall Have a Son
kicker: vv. 9–10
sub: Where Is Sarah Thy Wife?
scripture: Genesis 18:9-10 | mark: Sarah thy wife shall have a son
p: There, the Lord reiterated the promise and the blessing to Abraham, that he and Sarah will have a son. That their seed will bless all nations. We've covered that the seed is singular, Christ Jesus.

--- Sarah Laughed within Herself
kicker: vv. 11–12
sub: Old and Well Stricken in Age
scripture: Genesis 18:11-12 | mark: Therefore Sarah laughed within herself

--- Is Any Thing Too Hard for the LORD?
kicker: vv. 13–15
sub: Nay; but Thou Didst Laugh
scripture: Genesis 18:13-15 | mark: Is any thing too hard for the LORD?; Nay; but thou didst laugh
p: Sarah laughs, *After I am waxed old shall I have pleasure, my lord being old also?* and in a way familiar to us from the Gospels, and recognize in our walk with Him, He calls her on it and when she denies it in shame, He gently chides her, *Nay; but thou didst laugh.* There is nothing beyond what the Lord can do.

=== The cry of Sodom
--- Shall I Hide from Abraham?
kicker: vv. 16–19
sub: For I Know Him
scripture: Genesis 18:16-19 | mark: Shall I hide from Abraham that thing which I do; For I know him
p: Having finished the meal, the Lord God, Jesus ponders whether He shall tell Abraham of His intentions to judge Sodom and Gomorrah.

--- The Cry of Sodom and Gomorrah
kicker: vv. 20–21
sub: Their Sin Is Very Grievous
scripture: Genesis 18:20-21 | mark: Because the cry of Sodom and Gomorrah is great
p: That the cries of violence from the earth and the blood shed of the innocent had called out for His vengeance. Carrying out judgement and wrath.

=== Abraham intercedes
--- Shall Not the Judge of All the Earth Do Right?
kicker: vv. 22–25
sub: Wilt Thou Also Destroy the Righteous with the Wicked?
scripture: Genesis 18:22-25 | mark: Wilt thou also destroy the righteous with the wicked?; Shall not the Judge of all the earth do right?
p: Abraham understanding what's happening asks for the sake of the righteous, those who believe on the Lord for salvation, if some be found among the wicked, will He spare them?

--- Dust and Ashes
kicker: vv. 26–28
sub: Fifty, and Forty and Five
scripture: Genesis 18:26-28 | mark: which am but dust and ashes

--- For Ten's Sake
kicker: vv. 29–32
sub: Oh Let Not the LORD Be Angry
scripture: Genesis 18:29-32 | mark: I will not destroy it for ten’s sake
p: And the Lord, full of mercy and grace agrees if there were 50, 45, 40, even 10 righteous men, He would not destroy it for their sakes.

--- Abraham Returned unto His Place
kicker: v. 33
sub: The LORD Went His Way
big: Genesis 18:33
p: And the Lord and His angels go on their way, towards Sodom, and Abraham his way, returning to his place.

--- The Word of God
center: Here we see Christ Jesus as the word of God, the instrument of the Father's will.
